<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amadeus VIII, Duke of Savoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1383–1451</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Antipope Felix V</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amadeus VIII was count of Savoy from 1391 and was raised to duke by Emperor Sigismund in 1416. In 1418 he inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, uniting it with Savoy, and he issued a law code for his lands. He later retired to a hermitage and was elected antipope Felix V by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a> in 1439, resigning in 1449.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amadeus-viii-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="Amadeus VIII, Duke of Savoy" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amadeus_VIII_of_Savoy_from_a_French_edition_of_Albertanus_of_Brescia%27s_De_doctrina_dicendi_et_tacendi_and_De_amore_et_dilectione_Dei_et_proximi_et_aliarum_rerum_et_de_forma_vitae.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
